  "id": "Compound::DB00519 - Disease::DOID:10763",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that Trandolapril may be associated with Hypertension (disease) through a complex network of biological relationships. Trandolapril is linked to Coronary Artery Disease, which in turn is localized by Hypertension, indicating a potential causal pathway involving vascular pathology. Additionally, Trandolapril is shown to resemble Spirapril and Fosinopril, both of which are known to treat Hypertension (disease). This resemblance implies a structural or pharmacological similarity that could contribute to their therapeutic effects. The integration of these relationships highlights the role of Ace Inhibitors and Esters in the drug's mechanism of action, which are also implicated in the treatment of Hypertension. The evidence suggests that Trandolapril may exert its effects through mechanisms that are related to the treatment of Hypertension, though the exact nature of the relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
